gate: CLOSED
v:4 c:$ m:navitrack-config role:dev x:tauri
task: S20 T4 — Android init, then android:build
sprint: S20
dep: S20-T3-ios-init-and-build.pd
requires: [MOBILE_TAURI, BUN]
test_mandate: ../intel/TEST-COVERAGE-MANDATE.md
quality_mandate: ../intel/CODE-QUALITY-MANDATE.md
invariants: ../S20-INVARIANTS.md

context: |
  bun run android:build stops because src-tauri/gen/android does not exist.
  The SDK is at ~/Library/Android/sdk. ANDROID_HOME was unset.
  The CLI asks for tauri android init.
  For these commands set ANDROID_HOME to that SDK path.
  Do not commit a machine env file or secrets.
  Run bun run tauri android init. Do not commit gen/.
  Do not run the apk, aab, or open scripts. Do not upload to Play.
  Do not run live radio. Then bun run android:build with ANDROID_HOME set.
  If a new host error appears after gen/android exists, stop and record it.
  Do not guess a second fix. Package manager: bun. No pnpm or npm lockfile.

out:
  - gitignored Android project via tauri android init
  - append to sprints/S20/RELEASE-COMPILE.md

cmd:
  - bun run test
  - bun run android:build

done:
  - android:build compiles on this Mac with ANDROID_HOME set
  - gen/ is not committed
  - The note records the SDK path used and the result
  - No store upload and no live radio
  - `bun run test` passes
